From: arttttt <artem-bambalov@yandex.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] surfaceflinger: the composer draws the effects

On this device SurfaceFlinger composed on the GPU for one reason only in
the transition traces: rounded corners. The launcher's spring animation
back to home rounds the closing application's leash, the radius is
inherited by every child, and isClientCompositionForced hands the whole
group to RenderEngine -- 27-35 frames a run, 2.6 ms each on the main
thread, the commonest class of late frame left.

With ro.surface_flinger.hwc_draws_effects set, no effect forces client
composition any more -- rounded corners in OutputLayer; shadows, blur
and stretch in Layer. Only HDR Y410 still goes to the GPU. Every effect
is handed to the composer instead, as generic layer metadata, one key
each under org.lineageos.mocha.: rounded_corners, shadow, blur and
stretch, as floats; the layout is spelled out above
writeEffectsMetadata. Layer writes their rectangles and lengths in the
layer stack's space, and OutputLayer takes them into the display's on
the way out, as it does the display frame: the composer draws in the
panel's axes, which a turned display does not share with the layer
stack (stretch stays in the layer's own space, as RenderEngine takes
it). A key is sent only once the composer declares it,
so nothing reaches the composer that it would refuse, and then every
frame, all zero when the layer has no such effect, since generic
metadata cannot unset a key.

A composer that has not declared a key shows the layer without that
effect.

